# Shared shadcn UI

All client apps use one design system: `packages/ui` (`@brigada/ui`).

- Before writing markup, check whether a [shadcn](https://ui.shadcn.com) component exists (in the repo or addable via the CLI). If it does, use it.
- Add missing shadcn components into `@brigada/ui`, then import them. Do not copy components into an app.
- Do not build custom buttons, inputs, cards, dialogs, empty states, alerts, or similar primitives. Compose shadcn pieces instead.
- App files may add layout (`flex`, `gap`, page structure) only. No one-off styled replacements for registry components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom primitive
<button className="rounded-md bg-black px-4 py-2 text-white">Sign in</button>

// ✅ GOOD — shared shadcn
import { Button } from "@brigada/ui/components/button";

<Button>Sign in with Discord</Button>
```
